"s" to search.  If you've played for a while you should be able to
guess the most likely places to search.  Any one "s" has
something like a 1-in-14 chance of finding hidden doors, traps
and so on.

"^D" to kick.  This is very much a limited resource as you hurt
your legs kicking walls, but if there is a door there there's a
higher chance of finding it.

I like to go to the end of a corridor and kick straight.  Then do
some number of searches, then kick left, then some number of
searches, then kick right.  That'll cover teh end of the corridor.

I use a compromise strategy where I walk along a wall kicking
the likely seeming walls and searching the rest.



